## Paper metadata
- Title: Theory of analytical energy derivatives for the variational
  quantum eigensolver
- Authors: K. Mitarai, Y. O. Nakagawa, W. Mizukami
- arXiv: 1905.04054v2 (7 Jun 2019)
- Journal: Phys. Rev. Research 2, 013129 (2020)
- Open access: yes (arXiv preprint)

## Headline claim (paraphrased)
Analytical expressions and low-depth quantum circuits are given for VQE
energy derivatives (forces, force-constant matrices, spectroscopic
response tensors) for both ground and excited states. At the variational
optimum, first-order derivatives reduce to Hellmann-Feynman:

    dE/dR|_{theta=theta*} = <psi(theta*)| dH/dR |psi(theta*)>

sidestepping the noise-dominated failure of naive
reoptimize-VQE-at-R+/-dR finite differences on near-term devices.

## Numerical experiment reproduced
H2, STO-3G, r = 0.735 A, 4 qubits, 2-layer hardware-efficient ansatz.
Full details in `../report/REPORT.md` and `../report/REPORT.tex`.
